## Where your code goes

| You want to | Edit |
|---|---|
| Implement create/read/update/delete for a kind | `internal/controller/<kind>/external.go` |
| Build the API client from credentials | `internal/provider/client.go` |
| Add CLI flags or adjust controller options | `internal/provider/options.go` |
| Add fields to the ProviderConfig | `apis/v1alpha1/types.go` |
| Add fields to a managed resource | `apis/<group>/<version>/<kind>_types.go` |

## Names you must not rename

Tool-owned files call these. Renaming any of them breaks the build:

`provider.Client`, `provider.NewClient`, `provider.Flags`, `provider.Configure`,
`NewExternal`, `ReconcilerOptions`.

## Keeping up to date

Run `xp-provider-gen update` on a clean working tree. It refreshes the
tool-owned files, bumps the framework dependency versions, and leaves the
result uncommitted so you can review it with `git diff`. Your files are never
touched.

